Chapter: BootPaint

 The two definitions Core/PhaseAllocator.codex cites, and nothing else.

 Update 42 gave PhaseAllocator `cites Codex chapter BootPaint (bp-rtc-seconds,
 bp-log-phase)`. A cite names a CHAPTER rather than a symbol, so every subject
 carrying the real PhaseAllocator has to answer for a chapter of that name or
 plug-build-lib refuses the bundle with exit 3. It refuses correctly; the
 harness was the thing at fault for not listening.

 The real chapter is 341 lines that ground Device.Port and paint a progress
 strip onto a screen these subjects do not have. What PhaseAllocator actually
 wants from it is a clock reading and a log line, and it spends both on a
 report nothing in a subject reads.

 A stub is the honest choice here rather than the convenient one. Carrying the
 real chapter would put a WALL CLOCK inside the subject: phase-took would
 return however long that particular boot happened to take, so the emitted zig
 would differ between two identical builds and the fixed point could never
 hold. Zero is the only reading that keeps the artifact deterministic.

  bp-rtc-seconds : Integer -> Integer
  bp-rtc-seconds (mode) = 0

  bp-log-phase : Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bp-log-phase (label) (secs) (mb) = 0
